                <pb facs="0466" n="358" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg358"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Terres.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Foster, with reference to Mr. Terres’s dispatch of November 18, instructs him
                    to enter an earnest protest against the imprisonment of Mevs, if he has not
                    already been released, and to report by cable.</p>
            </div>
